<title>USA: Arthuis says G10 to welcome doubling of IMF's GAB.</title>
<headline>Arthuis says G10 to welcome doubling of IMF's GAB.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said Saturday that the Group of 10 was due to take account on Sunday of an agreement to double the IMF's General Arrangement to Borrow.</p>
<p>&quot;The agreements we are due to take note of tomorrow morning will allow the doubling of these resources.&quot;</p>
<p>The International Monetary Fund has pushed for the GAB, used to help countries facing serious financial crises, to be doubled to $50 billion.</p>
<p>The G10 is actually 11 nations. It is made up of the G7 countries -- Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the United States -- plus Switzerland, Sweden, Belgium and the Netherlands.</p>
